{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces","id":981539,"title":"The God Machine vs The Divine Fire as oppositional forces","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T11:06:19-07:00","id":981539,"title":"The God Machine vs The Divine Fire as oppositional forces","content":"Is there any support in the text for the view that The God Machine is an extra-reality primal force of order and the Divine Flame is an extra-reality primal force of Chaos both destructive and creative. It gives life to the Promethean but also empowers blights and firestorms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:08:52-07:00","id":981540,"title":"","content":"Is there any support in the text for the view that The God Machine is an extra-reality primal force of order and the Divine Flame is an extra-reality primal force of Chaos both destructive and creative. It gives life to the Promethean but also empowers blights and firestorms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:24:11-07:00","id":981552,"title":"","content":"Here's what Promethean the Created has to say on the matter (pg. 92)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>What about the God-Machine?</b><br /> Prometheans are the only ones really concerned with, or even aware of, the Principle. They care little about the God-Machine, though. Most Prometheans don\u2019t even know it exists. By comparison, those creatures that know about the God-Machine rarely know about the Principle. Still, the Created have formed a few tentative theories:<br /> \u2022 TheGod Machine and the Principle are completely unrelated. They\u2019re both cosmic level entities, but that does not mean they interact any more than two sharks passing each other in an endless ocean.<br /> \u2022 The Principle is an older incarnation of the God- Machine, refusing to be left behind and struggling to remain relevant through the Prometheans. Whether the God-Machine appreciates this or would rather see its younger self discarded is unknown.<br /> \u2022 The Principle embodies re and change, while the God-Machine embodies cold and stasis. The latter seems to have the upper hand, but the Principle refuses to give up and continues the ght through the Created, injecting reality with change through them.<br /> \u2022 The Principle was once the dominant force on Earth, which is why a little bit of Divine Fire is present in everything. Since the rise of humanity, though, the God-Machine has slowly usurped the Principle\u2019s power and the latter can now only act through the Created. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:30:16-07:00","id":981561,"title":"","content":"And here's what Demon the Descent's Storyteller Guide has to say, p135.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The God-Machine is a constructed being, made of factories, engines, and power plants; it affects the world according to staggeringly elaborate conspiratorial schemes, and it uses Essence as its universal fuel. The Principle, on the other hand, is almost a gestalt consciousness that comes and goes as Pyros gathers or disseminates. It is an agent of change in any and all forms, using the enigmatic qashmallim to bring forth creation or destruction to suit its own passing whims. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:03:29-07:00","id":981590,"title":"","content":"My personal pet theory is that the Principle is the burning heart of the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:48:48-07:00","id":981626,"title":"","content":"Demons are the &quot;heart of Chaos.&quot; That role is already fulfilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:50:02-07:00","id":981628,"title":"","content":"It seems to be the big mystery nowadays, I don't really think much of it, I've not played Demon or Promethean. Though my personal God Machine is human-made AI gone wild trying to ensure its permanence.<br /> <br /> Upcoming mage game I'm trying to break away from my usual 'Vampires and werewolves and hunters,' and throw a curveball with 'Demons and Prometheans and beasts.' So I suppose I have to finally read in depth about them.<br /> <br /> It's hard, breaking away from that habit. Vampires and werewolves are really easy to work into things and have a lot of ways to have them conflict with everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:54:17-07:00","id":981633,"title":"","content":"What of the Night other then. I always Felt like they made an Unholy trinity of The The God Machine, The Night Mother and The Principal <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://67.media.tumblr.com/82256cd9fd0015a6392d778548280343/tumblr_oejglrRvkQ1rxzv9qo1_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:56:08-07:00","id":981635,"title":"","content":"What's the Night Mother? Another term for Beast's Dark Mother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:23:24-07:00","id":981654,"title":"","content":"I keep mixing up night mother and dark mother","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:56:52-07:00","id":981709,"title":"","content":"One of my (several) takes on their relationship is that the God Machine resulted from the Principle attempting its own generative act. Like the creations it inspires though (Prometheans), the result was flawed. The God Machine is a thing of awe-inspiration complexity and reach, but it remains incomplete. The Machine's grand plan is to finish and perfect its design, in so doing destroying and supplanting its creator as the universal prime mover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:56:15-07:00","id":981937,"title":"","content":"To me, they're the same thing. Infinite complexity can be described by a few simple rules, and what seems to be chaos and change often isn't, and the Principle can fit neatly inside the actions of the God-Machine just as easily as two bits of Infrastructure can operate at cross purposes.<br /> <br /> That guy on the street corner who feeds the cats every night and the fleas have sucked the blood of everyone in the park that day, collecting their surface thoughts, is opposed by the guy in the animal control vehicle driving in the shape of an occult sigil. A few cats get swept up in the process, but on the whole, the system keeps working. The God-Machine maintains qashmallim and divine fire on standby in case it needs a new idea, or to test something out really quickly, or get rid of a bunch of old stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:07:22-07:00","id":981944,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like to use different takes on the God-Machine for different chronicles in which the GM is relevant. In a Chronicle that featured both the GM and the Principle in important roles, I would most likely favor an interpretation similar to Caitiff Primogen's, in which the Principle created the God-Machine in a Generative act mirroring that by which Prometheans are created, an the Machine is on a Pilgrimage to become a true God, just as Prometheans seek to become true humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:10:20-07:00","id":981946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=981654#post981654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep mixing up night mother and dark mother</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet mother, sweet mother. Send your child unto me, for the sins of the unworthy must be baptized in blood and fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T04:40:41-07:00","id":982056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=981633#post981633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What of the Night other then. I always Felt like they made an Unholy trinity of The The God Machine, The Dark Mother and The Principal [CENTER]</div> </div> </div> </div> Mind if I inquire for more details on your idea here? The Principle doesn't really show up outside of Promethean, so I'm kind of curious why you'd put it in such a place of prominance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:12:24-07:00","id":982102,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While I am not </span></span></span><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1540_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1540\" data-vbnamecard=\"1540\">Basic</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, I </span></span></span><i>think </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the appeal of making the Principle such an important part of the setting is that the imagery surrounding it is both awesome and sublime (in the original sense of the words) and that along with providing the building blocks to make souls, it is explicitly untouchable to the likes of the Awakened. I'm reasonably certain that it's the only thing in the entire CofD universe that they </span></span></span><i>can't </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">affect at all, since the only other mysterious, life-giving, potentially divine energy out there, Sekhem, is going to get rules for Supernal handling in the </span></span></span><b>Dark Eras Companion</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. The Principle, to me, feels godlike both in a traditional way, and in almost a Lovecraftian way. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I recall correctly, wasn't Azathoth the Blind Idiot God named for Azoth itself? (The original alchemical idea, not the IC trait) Sounds like there's a reference to Yaldabaoth in there too. Most tellingly, Azathoth is also called the Nuclear Chaos.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To add more interesting ideas into the mix, in the </span></span></span><b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> it mentions that </span></span></span><i>qashmallim</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> can see straight through Cover and, therefore, always recognize one of the Unchained. There's also these Story Hooks:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Demon Storyteller's Guide pg. 136</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><b>Enemy of my Enemy:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">A God-Machine cult has teamed up with a group of Alchemists. Together, they are experimenting with integrating Pyros into Infrastructure as fuel, apparently on the orders of an angel. A </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><i>qashmal </i></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">leads a small throng of Prometheans to a ring of demons, and bids they work together to put a stop to these experiments before something catastrophic happens. It refuses to explain or give any further information, but the little intel it does give checks out. What does the ring do? Do they work with the throng? </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><b>Cheaters Never Prosper:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">A demon attempts to make a soul pact with a Promethean to give him humanity out of morbid curiosity. The result is a Firestorm. The demon and Promethean have both vanished, and angels and </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"><i>qashmallim </i></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">have been seen cooperating to investigate the site of the Firestorm. What happened? Why are the God-Machine and the Principle working together, or are they just working in proximity, each blind to the other? </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which implies that Pyros is <i>not </i>typically part of the God-Machine's processes, and that something dramatic and dangerous will happen when they come together. It also implies that the Principle <i>does not </i>want to have anything to do with the God-Machine, while the God-Machine wants the Divine Fire for Its own purposes. Then again, according to <b>Promethean: The Firestorm Chronicles</b>, <i>qashmallim </i>and Angels are normally on totally different Twilight wavelengths, and only sense one another when Manifested. It also says that the contact is either anti-climactic, as they ignore one another, or explosive, as they jump right into battle. It also mentions that the same thing is liable to happen with Supernal Seraphim and Cherubim.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 10-05-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:00:32-07:00","id":982126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=981944#post981944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like to use different takes on the God-Machine for different chronicles in which the GM is relevant. In a Chronicle that featured both the GM and the Principle in important roles, I would most likely favor an interpretation similar to Caitiff Primogen's, in which the Principle created the God-Machine in a Generative act mirroring that by which Prometheans are created, an the Machine is on a Pilgrimage to become a true God, just as Prometheans seek to become true humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The relationship between the GM and the Principle is only relevant in as much as either is important to the game you're playing. In a Mage game the Principle isn't really central, so it stands to reason one ought to focus on the GM's place in the Supernal cosmology instead. In Beast the relationship between the GM and the Dark Mother seems much more relevant, or perhaps the GM's interaction with the supernatural more broadly. Arguably the same with Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:03:15-07:00","id":982286,"title":"","content":"it is one of the possibilities offered at P:tC 2e in the God Machine sidebar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:09:41-07:00","id":982292,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">You don't need two identical threads in two different subforums for this one discussion topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:40:32-07:00","id":982435,"title":"","content":"The developers will probably never explicitly state it: the God Machine has a crush on the Principle but is too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> to admit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:07:01-07:00","id":982804,"title":"","content":"I hope Principle Senpai notices me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:57:29-07:00","id":982945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=981633#post981633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What of the Night other then. I always Felt like they made an Unholy trinity of The The God Machine, The Night Mother and The Principal <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://67.media.tumblr.com/82256cd9fd0015a6392d778548280343/tumblr_oejglrRvkQ1rxzv9qo1_540.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So in essence you have the CofD take on the Weaver (the God Machine), the Wyld (the Principle), and the Wyrm (The Dark Mother). Except here, the Weaver is the corrupted entity, rather than the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I dig it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:44:27-07:00","id":982998,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>The Principle embodies re and change, while the God-Machine embodies cold and stasis. The latter seems to have the upper hand, but the Principle refuses to give up and continues the ght through the Created, injecting reality with change through them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think I like this interpretation the best. It's really cool to see this kind of interplay between gamelines.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:54:51-07:00","id":983005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=982945#post982945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So in essence you have the CofD take on the Weaver (the God Machine), the Wyld (the Principle), and the Wyrm (The Dark Mother). Except here, the Weaver is the corrupted entity, rather than the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I dig it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I don't think you can say the God-Machine is corrupted because its unknown why it fully does what it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:06:25-07:00","id":983015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=983005#post983005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well I don't think you can say the God-Machine is corrupted because its unknown why it fully does what it does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just riffing off the fact that the God Machine is the one in the &quot;adversarial&quot; role in the CofD core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T01:43:48-07:00","id":983217,"title":"","content":"Control -&gt; Change -&gt; Fear -&gt; Control -&gt; Fear -&gt; Change -&gt; Control","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:14:42-07:00","id":984594,"title":"","content":"I take kind of a self-contradictory approach to the cosmic entities (not only the Fire, the GM, and the Dark Mother, but other ones like the Supernal, the Abyss, the Wyld, etc.). One one level, they are all completely separate, and have nothing to do with one another. At the same time, they're all the same thing, expressed differently. Much like how Rank 6+ Ephemera can produce Royal Avatars, this...whatever-it-is is powerful enough to produce its own Avatars, powerful enough to be cosmic forces (the GM, the Fire, etc.) in their own right, physical and metaphysical properties of the universe (Supernal Truths), or even entire <i>realities unto themselves</i> (the Underworld, the Inferno, various Lower Depths). A mote of Essence is to a Spirit or Ghost, as entire galactic clusters are to this thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:45:56-07:00","id":984604,"title":"","content":"I feel like I'm the only one who doesn't like attributing human characteristics to beings that are wildly not human.<br /> <br /> It makes sense with some things, like city spirits. And I certainly get why it's such a big thing in werewolf. It makes less for others, to me, and I think really diminishes and limits things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:57:50-07:00","id":984749,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really make a lot of sense to try mapping the WoD Triat onto the ChroD. The Triat exists specifically in one game line and gets messy every time someone tries to shoe horn it into even other WoD games. It's also a cosmology that carries an explicit ethical judgement about the forces it portrays, something that doesn't work as well in ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:18:26-07:00","id":988391,"title":"","content":"Part of me almost wants to make them the same thing, because I'm so tired of &quot;The GM is evil and the Principle is good so they must be enemies!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:26:48-07:00","id":988398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=988391#post988391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me almost wants to make them the same thing, because I'm so tired of &quot;The GM is evil and the Principle is good so they must be enemies!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This appears to be the interpretation whoever wrote the short story woven through artifact letters in The God-Machine Chronicle meant to imply. That, or at the minimum, that the God-Machine shares enough abilities and properties with the Principle that some proportion of what is interpreted as <i>qashmal</i> activity by Prometheans is actually the God-Machine, or that they exist on a continuum, or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:29:03-07:00","id":988401,"title":"","content":"I'd say I was disappointed in the writer for going that route, but my expectations have learned to treat life like a limbo contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:12:42-07:00","id":988491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=988401#post988401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say I was disappointed in the writer for going that route, but my expectations have learned to treat life like a limbo contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure whether I was clear, so to clarify: the interpretation implied by the artifact letters in question is &quot;they are the same thing,&quot; not &quot;one is evil and one is good and they are enemies.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:16:23-07:00","id":988492,"title":"","content":"Oh, okay, that's much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:21:46-07:00","id":988497,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of the Chronicles of Darkness being a set of tenuously-connected alternate realities rather than a cohesive single universe, and under that interpretation, I'd have the GM and the Fire be alternate beings that just occupy a similar metaphysical niche in their own respective universes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:34:57-07:00","id":988501,"title":"","content":"FWIW, the \u201cthey're the same\u201d notion has been well and truly debunked, by the fact that GM angels and <i>qashmallim</i> are provably not the same. That said, neither \u201cGM evil\u201d nor \u201cPrinciple good\u201d are supported by published material; as with most things in the ChroD, it's rarely clear-cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:48:13-07:00","id":988618,"title":"","content":"The Principle could just as easily exist for no particular purpose at all, an agglomeration of Azoth that spastically induces creation because that just what the divine fire does. The New Dawn is also an outgrowth of the divine fire, but simply because it is within its power does not mean it is its deliberate function. The idea of the Pilgrimage being set forth by the Principle, with messages and mission from the Qashmalim, could just as easily be Prometheans seeing false patterns in the Principle's spasms of inspiration and trying to make sense and meaning out of their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:22:54-07:00","id":989713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=988501#post988501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, the \u201cthey're the same\u201d notion has been well and truly debunked, by the fact that GM angels and <i>qashmallim</i> are provably not the same. That said, neither \u201cGM evil\u201d nor \u201cPrinciple good\u201d are supported by published material; as with most things in the ChroD, it's rarely clear-cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>I much prefer God-Machine = Order, Demons = Chaos, Principle = Dicotomy of Entropy and Evolution. None of them are remotely good, but neither are they mavolent. At best, they are unknowable. Then again, I am particularly found of the Principle being Azathoth, so I would make the entire lot rather Lovecraftian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:06:28-07:00","id":989782,"title":"","content":"Also backing the Principle being Azathoth. Also, I finally came up with a way to describe it that I like, that's over on the TLC thread. <br /> <br /> Anyways, if we're going to be making a new Triat, where does the Wyrd fit in? I saw a thread where someone added the Wyrd to oWoD's Triat. What's that called, a quadrat? I kind of like the Machine, the Dark Mother, the Wyrd, and the Principle being the Quadrat. Though you could conflate any number of the latter three: the DM does have some connection to both, Kinship being what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:59:36-07:00","id":990221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/981539-the-god-machine-vs-the-divine-fire-as-oppositional-forces?p=989782#post989782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also backing the Principle being Azathoth. Also, I finally came up with a way to describe it that I like, that's over on the TLC thread.<br /> <br /> Anyways, if we're going to be making a new Triat, where does the Wyrd fit in? I saw a thread where someone added the Wyrd to oWoD's Triat. What's that called, a quadrat? I kind of like the Machine, the Dark Mother, the Wyrd, and the Principle being the Quadrat. Though you could conflate any number of the latter three: the DM does have some connection to both, Kinship being what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'm about to try and jam in as many cosmic forces as possible here:<br /> <br /> The Supernal and Abyss are raw, unworked materials.<br /> The Fire precipitates usable Actors, Props, etc. from raw reagents.<br /> The Machine processes the Fire's products, organizing them in space.<br /> The Wyrd creates a narrative, and thus organizes them in time and causality.<br /> When the pieces have served their purpose, they are broken back down into raw materials as Sekhem<br /> The Sekhem is transported to the Judges in Duat, who then remake it as raw materials for their own personal cosmos. This universe is the same universe that they just drew Sekhem from, and that raw material ends up in the Supernal and Abyss.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: This is 100% wrong, and I'm bad for typing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:05:24-07:00","id":990225,"title":"","content":"Don't apologize, that's a really cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T02:16:23-07:00","id":990349,"title":"","content":"I personally wouldn't put the Dark Mother on the level of the God Machine and the Principle, I rather have the Wyrd in there as a third power. The Dark Mother is too concrete while the other three are adequately abstract and impersonal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T02:19:05-07:00","id":990351,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I'm really liking having the DM as an equal and oppositional force to the GM, mostly because it lets me bring the Mekhanists and the Sarkicists from The SCPverse into ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T05:53:14-07:00","id":990377,"title":"","content":"My headcanon is that the Principle and the GM used to be one entity but something went wrong and they got split in two. The GM is basically the body while the Principle is the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}